From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: allow production PON row activity updates

Production sessions use hardware row timestamps to refresh netfilter flow
lifetimes. Static rows forward packets but retain their installation timestamp,
so an active session expires after the flowtable timeout. Clear STATIC when
building the owned bound row so packet hits update its activity timestamp.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu_production.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu_production.h
@@ -228,8 +228,9 @@
 		goto fail;
 	}
 	bound = owner->production.data;
-	bound.ib1 &= ~(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATE | AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TIMESTAMP);
-	bound.ib1 |= AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATIC |
+	bound.ib1 &= ~(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATE | AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TIMESTAMP |
+		       AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATIC);
+	bound.ib1 |=
 		FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATE, AIROHA_FOE_STATE_BIND) |
 		FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TIMESTAMP, airoha_ppe_get_timestamp(ppe));
 	spin_lock_bh(&ppe_lock);
